{"id": "unknown-2026-08-13-001", "date": "2026-08-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["[否定]growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam's textile boom may not translate into apparel growth", "content": "Vietnam’s textile and garment exports reached $4,672 million in July 2026, up 4.3 per cent year on year; the seven-month total was $27.02 billion, up 2.67 per cent.\nGrowth was concentrated upstream as garments, the volume anchor, grew just 0.7 per cent.\nVietnam faces a 20 per cent US apparel tariff, while US apparel imports from Vietnam rose only 1.4 per cent in January–May 2026.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-textile-boom-may-not-translate-into-apparel-growth-312606-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-13-002", "date": "2026-08-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India ITME 2026 roadshow begins with Coimbatore curtain-raiser", "content": "India ITME Society has launched its campaign for India ITME 2026 with a curtain-raiser in Coimbatore.\nScheduled for December 4–9 in Greater Noida, the event expects over 1,800 exhibitors, participation from 95-plus countries and over 150,000 visitors.\nIt will showcase advanced textile machinery, sustainable manufacturing and next-generation technologies.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-itme-2026-roadshow-begins-with-coimbatore-curtain-raiser-312568-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-13-003", "date": "2026-08-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["leading", "growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "India's Q1 FY27 GDP growth seen at 8%: SBI Research", "content": "SBI Research expects India’s real GDP growth at about 8 per cent in Q1 FY27, above the RBI projection of 7 per cent.\nThe nowcast cites broad-based momentum, with 86 per cent of over 50 leading indicators accelerating versus 69 per cent a year earlier.\nFor textile exporters and apparel sourcing teams, resilient demand, capex and credit trends point to a supportive near-term market.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-q1-fy27-gdp-growth-seen-at-8-sbi-research-312584-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-13-004", "date": "2026-08-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "India loses $1.25 bn in T&A export orders from US in H1 2026", "content": "India’s T&A exports to the US fell 23.3 per cent YoY to around $4.10 billion in H1 2026, from $5.35 billion a year earlier. \nIts calculated US import-market share slipped to around 8.6 per cent from 10.4 per cent, a loss of about 1.8 percentage points. \nASEAN shipments rose 4.5 per cent to $15.34 billion, while Bangladesh marginally exceeded India at around $4.12 billion. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-loses-1-25-bn-in-t-a-export-orders-from-us-in-h1-2026-312574-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-13-005", "date": "2026-08-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India retains BBB- rating as Fitch flags robust growth prospects", "content": "Fitch affirmed India’s BBB- sovereign rating with a Stable Outlook, citing robust growth, solid external finances and stability.\nFor textile and apparel exporters, manufacturers and sourcing teams, this points to resilient growth and contained inflation.\nFY27 GDP growth is forecast at 6.4 per cent and inflation at 4.1 per cent, while energy shocks, high debt and debt service remain constraints.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-retains-bbb-rating-as-fitch-flags-robust-growth-prospects-312577-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-13-006", "date": "2026-08-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Adopt fair trading practices to take 'Make in India' global: Goyal", "content": "Commerce Minister Piyush Goyal urged fair trading practices, recycling, reuse and circular-economy participation to strengthen the Make in India brand globally.\nHe said nine free trade agreements have opened markets for Indian industry, supporting preferential access for exporters and MSMEs.\nWith exports at a record $863 trillion last year, Goyal set a $1 trillion target for the current year.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/adopt-fair-trading-practices-to-take-make-in-india-global-goyal-312601-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-13-007", "date": "2026-08-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh AmCham targets over $5 bn in US investment", "content": "AmCham Bangladesh aims to mobilise over $5 billion in extra US investment over five years for Bangladesh’s investment pipeline.\nIt backed FY2026-27 reforms on approvals, Single Window, tax, VAT, repatriation and customs, while seeking policy predictability.\nFor apparel and textile sourcing chains, the US-Bangladesh trade framework could support stronger global value-chain positioning.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-amcham-targets-over-5-bn-in-us-investment-312590-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-13-008", "date": "2026-08-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US' Kontoor Brands Q2 revenue up 19% on Helly Hansen boost", "content": "American apparel and workwear group Kontoor Brands reported a 19 per cent YoY rise in Q2 FY26 revenue to $584 million, supported by Helly Hansen and Wrangler growth. \nAdjusted operating income increased 19 per cent to $94 million, while EPS rose 13 per cent to $1.06. \nThe company raised its FY26 outlook, projecting revenue of $2.66–2.71 billion and higher adjusted EPS. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-kontoor-brands-q2-revenue-up-19-on-helly-hansen-boost-312611-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-13-009", "date": "2026-08-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh apparel suppliers press US buyers on tariff refunds", "content": "Bangladeshi garment exporters are pressing US buyers for compensation after absorbing part of 2025 reciprocal tariff costs through price cuts and discounts. \nUS importers are receiving refunds after the Supreme Court ruled against the tariff regime. \nSuppliers may seek recovery through higher prices, larger orders, concessions or legal claims under LDP terms. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-apparel-suppliers-press-us-buyers-on-tariff-refunds-312595-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
